silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_01_signature_calculus_sections_02_algebra_category_concrete_anchor a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "AlgebraCategoryConcreteAnchorExample" .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_01_signature_calculus_sections_02_algebra_category_concrete_anchor silm:hasExample "In 'AlgebraCategoryConcreteAnchor', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, ColimitAlgebra_MittensColimitApex: the pair (MittensColimitApex, colimit_alpha: Sigma(MittensColimitApex) -> MittensColimitApex); the Sigma-algebra whose carrier is the colimit apex and whose structure map colimit_alpha assembles the twelve tagged legs into the colimit; also, T_Sigma_VetRecord_77: the free Sigma-algebra generated by VetRecord_77; equals PublishTreeType specialized to VetRecord_77 as the leaf; the free monad T_Sigma applied to the set {VetRecord_77}; every element is a publish tree with VetRecord_77 at the leaves; also, CataMorphism_VetRecord_Colimit: the unique Sigma-algebra homomorphism cata(colimit_alpha): (PublishTreeType, in_Sigma) -> (MittensColimitApex, colimit_alpha); the morphism in Alg(Sigma) that folds the publish tree into the colimit element." .
